{"id": "section-body-04376", "title": "Leishmaniasis", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Protozoa and Others", "Leishmaniasis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04376", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Leishmaniasis", "runs": [{"text": "Leishmaniasis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1760"}}, {"id": "body-04377", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Leishmaniasis is a parasitic disease caused by protozoans of the genus Leishmania, transmitted primarily by the bite of infected female phlebotomine sandflies. It presents in three main forms cutaneous, mucocutaneous, and visceral.", "runs": [{"text": "Leishmaniasis is a parasitic disease caused by protozoans of the genus Leishmania, transmitted primarily by the bite of infected female phlebotomine sandflies. It presents in three main forms cutaneous, mucocutaneous, and visceral."}]}, {"id": "body-04378", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Visceral leishmaniasis (VL), also known as kala-azar, is fatal if left untreated in over 95% of cases. It is characterized by irregular bouts of fever, weight loss, enlargement of the spleen and liver, and anaemia. Most cases occur in Brazil, east Africa and India.", "runs": [{"text": "Visceral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leishmaniasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(VL),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "also"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "known"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "kala-azar,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fatal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "left"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "untreated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "over"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "95%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "irregular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bouts"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weight"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loss,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enlargement"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spleen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "liver,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anaemia."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Most"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Brazil, east Africa and India."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04379", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Cutaneous leishmaniasis (CL) is the most common form and causes skin lesions, mainly ulcers, on exposed parts of the body. These can leave life-long scars and cause serious disability or stigma. About 95% of CL cases occur in the Americas, the Mediterranean basin, the Middle East and central Asia. Mucocutaneous leishmaniasis (MCL) leads to partial or total destruction of mucous membranes of the nose, mouth and throat. Over 90% of mucocutaneous leishmaniasis cases occur in Bolivia, Brazil, Ethiopia and Peru.", "runs": [{"text": "Cutaneous leishmaniasis (CL) is the most common form and causes skin lesions, mainly ulcers, on exposed parts of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "These"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leave"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "life-long"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scars"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cause"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "serious"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disability"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stigma."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "About"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "95%"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CL"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Americas,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Mediterranean"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "basin,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Middle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "East"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "central"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Asia."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Mucocutaneous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leishmaniasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(MCL)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leads to partial or total destruction of mucous membranes of the nose, mouth and throat. Over 90% of mucocutaneous leishmaniasis cases occur in Bolivia, Brazil, Ethiopia and Peru."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04382", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case Definitions Suspected Case:", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Definitions Suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Case:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04383", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "CL: Presence of characteristic skin lesions in a person from an endemic area, persisting for weeks to months, with or without a history of sandfly exposure.", "runs": [{"text": "CL: Presence of characteristic skin lesions in a person from an endemic area, persisting for weeks to months, with or without a history of sandfly exposure."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04384", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "MCL: Mucosal lesions (nasal, oral, or pharyngeal) with or without a history of CL, in an endemic area.", "runs": [{"text": "MCL:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Mucosal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lesions"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(nasal,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oral,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pharyngeal)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "without"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CL,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "endemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "area."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04385", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "VL: Prolonged fever (>2 weeks), weight loss, and splenomegaly in a person from an endemic area or with travel history to such areas.", "runs": [{"text": "VL: Prolonged fever (>2 weeks), weight loss, and splenomegaly in a person from an endemic area or with travel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history to such areas."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04387", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Probable Case: Suspected case with epidemiological link (e.g., travel to endemic area) and positive serology (e.g., rK39 rapid test for VL) or suggestive histopathology.", "runs": [{"text": "Probable", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "epidemiological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "link"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "travel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "endemic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "area)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "positive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "serology"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rK39"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rapid test for VL) or suggestive histopathology."}]}, {"id": "body-04389", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Confirmed Case:", "runs": [{"text": "Confirmed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Case:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04390", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "CL/MCL: Demonstration of Leishmania parasites in tissue samples (e.g., skin biopsy, smear, or culture) or positive PCR.", "runs": [{"text": "CL/MCL: Demonstration of Leishmania parasites in tissue samples (e.g., skin biopsy, smear, or culture) or positive "}, {"text": "PCR."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04391", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "VL: Parasites identified in bone marrow, spleen, or lymph node aspirates, or positive PCR or serology (e.g., direct agglutination test, rK39) in the presence of clinical signs.", "runs": [{"text": "VL: Parasites identified in bone marrow, spleen, or lymph node aspirates, or positive PCR or serology (e.g., direct agglutination test, rK39) in the presence of clinical signs."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04392", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "PKDL: Clinical signs with parasitological or molecular confirmation, often in a patient with a history of VL.", "runs": [{"text": "PKDL:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parasitological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "molecular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmation,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "history"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " VL."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1752"}}, {"id": "body-04394", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04395", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The treatment of leishmaniasis depends on several factors including type of disease, concomitant pathologies, parasite species and geographic location. Leishmaniasis is a treatable and curable disease, which requires an immunocompetent system because medicines will not get rid of the parasite from the body, thus the risk of relapse if immunosuppression occurs. All patients diagnosed with visceral leishmaniasis require prompt and complete treatment.", "runs": [{"text": "The treatment of leishmaniasis depends on several factors including type of disease, concomitant pathologies, parasite species and geographic location. Leishmaniasis is a treatable and curable disease, which requires an immunocompetent system"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "because"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medicines"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "will"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "get"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parasite"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "thus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relapse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immunosuppression"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurs. All patients diagnosed with visceral leishmaniasis require prompt and complete treatment."}]}, {"id": "body-04397", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Visceral leishmaniasis caused by L. donovani in East Africa", "runs": [{"text": "Visceral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leishmaniasis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "L."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "donovani"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "East"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Africa"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04398", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "S: liposomal amphotericin B(IV):3–5mg/kg 24hourly by infusion giv